<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xml:lang="en"><generator uri="https://jekyllrb.com/" version="4.3.3">Jekyll</generator><link href="https://kamilov.io/feed.xml" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml"/><link href="https://kamilov.io/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en"/><updated>2026-10-24T03:46:09+00:00</updated><id>https://kamilov.io/feed.xml</id><title type="html">blank</title><subtitle>Ulugbek S. Kamilov is a Professor of Computational Imaging at UW–Madison, working on inverse problems, plug-and-play priors, and deep learning for imaging.</subtitle><entry><title type="html">Blog Post Template</title><link href="https://kamilov.io/blog/2026/blog-template/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Blog Post Template"/><published>2026-10-23T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-10-23T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://kamilov.io/blog/2026/blog-template</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://kamilov.io/blog/2026/blog-template/"><![CDATA[<p>This post shows the main building blocks of an al-folio blog post. Copy it as a starting point for new posts.</p> <h2 id="text-formatting">Text formatting</h2> <p>Text can be <strong>bold</strong>, <em>italic</em>, or <strong><em>both</em></strong>.</p> <h3 id="lists">Lists</h3> <ul> <li>Bullet lists start each line with a dash</li> <li>Indent by two spaces to nest <ul> <li>like this</li> </ul> </li> </ul> <ol> <li>Numbered lists start each line with a number</li> <li>The numbers are renumbered automatically</li> </ol> <h3 id="quotes-and-dividers">Quotes and dividers</h3> <blockquote> <p>Blockquotes start each line with <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">&gt;</code>. Use them for quotations or to set a remark apart.</p> </blockquote> <p>A horizontal rule (three dashes on their own line) separates sections:</p> <hr/> <h2 id="links">Links</h2> <p>Read more about <a href="https://jekyllrb.com/">Jekyll</a>, or see the <a href="/publications/">publications page</a>.</p> <h2 id="code">Code</h2> <p>Inline code looks like <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">numpy.linalg.norm(x)</code>. A code block with syntax highlighting:</p> <div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">numpy</span> <span class="k">as</span> <span class="n">np</span>


<span class="k">def</span> <span class="nf">soft_threshold</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">x</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">tau</span><span class="p">):</span>
    <span class="sh">"""</span><span class="s">Proximal operator of the l1 norm.</span><span class="sh">"""</span>
    <span class="k">return</span> <span class="n">np</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">sign</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">x</span><span class="p">)</span> <span class="o">*</span> <span class="n">np</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">maximum</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">np</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">abs</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">x</span><span class="p">)</span> <span class="o">-</span> <span class="n">tau</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="mf">0.0</span><span class="p">)</span>


<span class="nf">print</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="nf">soft_threshold</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">np</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">array</span><span class="p">([</span><span class="o">-</span><span class="mf">2.0</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="mf">0.5</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="mf">3.0</span><span class="p">]),</span> <span class="mf">1.0</span><span class="p">))</span>
</code></pre></div></div> <h2 id="math">Math</h2> <p>Inline math sits inside a sentence, like \(y = Ax + e\) for a linear measurement model.</p> <p>A displayed equation goes in its own paragraph:</p> \[\hat{x} = \arg\min_{x} \left\{ \frac{1}{2} \|y - Ax\|_2^2 + \lambda \|x\|_1 \right\}\] <h2 id="image">Image</h2> <div class="row justify-content-sm-center"> <div class="col-sm-6 mt-3 mt-md-0"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/kamilov-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/kamilov-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/kamilov-1400.webp 1400w," sizes="95vw" type="image/webp"/> <img src="/assets/img/kamilov.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" alt="Portrait of Ulugbek Kamilov" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> <figcaption class="caption">A figure with a caption, added with figure.liquid.</figcaption> </figure> </div> </div> <h2 id="table">Table</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th style="text-align: left">Method</th> <th style="text-align: center">Type</th> <th style="text-align: right">Year</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td style="text-align: left">ISTA</td> <td style="text-align: center">Iterative</td> <td style="text-align: right">2004</td> </tr> <tr> <td style="text-align: left">ADMM</td> <td style="text-align: center">Iterative</td> <td style="text-align: right">2011</td> </tr> <tr> <td style="text-align: left">PnP-ADMM</td> <td style="text-align: center">Learned</td> <td style="text-align: right">2013</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id="citation">Citation</h2> <p>Measurement score-based diffusion models are introduced in <a class="citation" href="#Park.etal2026">(Park et al., 2026)</a>.</p> <h2 id="references">References</h2> <div class="publications"> <h2 class="bibliography">2026</h2> <ol class="bibliography"><li> <div class="row" data-category="selective" data-award="false"> <div class="col col-sm-2 abbr"> <abbr class="badge rounded w-100"> <a href="https://iclr.cc">ICLR</a> </abbr> </div> <div id="Park.etal2026" class="col-sm-8"> <div class="title">Measurement Score-Based Diffusion Model</div> <div class="author"> C. Y. Park,&nbsp;S. Shoushtari,&nbsp;and&nbsp;<em>U. S. Kamilov</em> </div> <div class="periodical"> <em>In Int. Conf. Learn. Represent. (ICLR)</em>, 2026 </div> <div class="periodical"> </div> <div class="links"> <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.11853" class="btn btn-sm z-depth-0" role="button">arXiv</a> <a class="bibtex btn btn-sm z-depth-0" role="button">Bib</a> <a href="https://openreview.net/forum?id=pFByPVh6bd" class="btn btn-sm z-depth-0" role="button">HTML</a> <a href="https://github.com/wustl-cig/measurement_diffusion" class="btn btn-sm z-depth-0" role="button">Code</a> <a href="https://wustl-cig.github.io/msmwww/" class="btn btn-sm z-depth-0" role="button">Website</a> </div> <div class="bibtex hidden"> <figure class="highlight"><pre><code class="language-bibtex" data-lang="bibtex"><span class="nc">@inproceedings</span><span class="p">{</span><span class="nl">Park.etal2026</span><span class="p">,</span>
  <span class="na">author</span> <span class="p">=</span> <span class="s">{Park, C. Y. and Shoushtari, S. and Kamilov, U. S.}</span><span class="p">,</span>
